{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1763553,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"red-dark_un","paid":0,"title":"All-In Put","festival_id":null,"organization_id":1173891,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-09-30T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-09T00:00:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/all-in-put-indian-institute-of-information-technology-iiit-kottayam-1763553","region":"offline","details":"<p><strong>Overview:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>A team-based electronics and innovation event where participants bid for components using virtual credits and then build their own creative working project using the resources they acquire.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Eligibility:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to undergraduate students from any branch\/specialization.<\/li>\n<li>Inter-college teams are allowed.<\/li>\n<li>Inter-specialization teams are allowed.<\/li>\n<li>Team size: 3 - 5 members.<\/li>\n<li>A participant can be part of only one team.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Format:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Each team receives a fixed amount of virtual credits.<\/li>\n<li>Common\/basic components are to be bought using these credits.<\/li>\n<li>Special\/limited components are auctioned and can be bought using remaining credits after buying the basic components.<\/li>\n<li>Teams must strategically bid and manage their budget.<\/li>\n<li>After the auction, teams can build any project they want using only the components\/resources they acquired.<\/li>\n<li>Teams design, assemble, program and demonstrate their project.<\/li>\n<li>Projects are evaluated based on functionality, creativity, technical implementation and efficient use of resources.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Auction:<\/strong> 1.5-2 hours<\/li>\n<li><strong>Build &amp; Design:<\/strong> 2.5 hours<\/li>\n<li><strong>Final Demonstration &amp; Evaluation:<\/strong> 30 minutes<\/li>\n<li><strong>Total Duration:<\/strong> Approximately 6 hours.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Rules:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Each team will receive the same initial amount of virtual credits.<\/li>\n<li>Teams must use only the components\/resources they have acquired through the permitted event mechanisms.<\/li>\n<li>Teams may not secretly obtain components from other teams or external sources.<\/li>\n<li>Any resource trade must be approved by the event coordinators.<\/li>\n<li>Components cannot be exchanged after the trading period closes.<\/li>\n<li>Teams must not interfere with another team's circuit, code, components, or workspace.<\/li>\n<li>Any attempt to gain an unfair advantage through unauthorized hardware, software, communication, or external assistance may result in disqualification.<\/li>\n<li>Only low-voltage components supplied\/approved by the organizers may be used.<\/li>\n<li>Teams are responsible for handling the components assigned to them.<\/li>\n<li>The organizers' decision regarding rule violations and scoring will be final.<\/li>\n<li>Any resource trade must be approved by the event coordinators.<\/li>\n<li>Components cannot be exchanged after the trading period closes.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Objective:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>To encourage participants to think creatively, make strategic engineering decisions and develop a functional project under limited resources, budget and time constraints.<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Registration Fee:<\/strong> Rs.250 per team<\/li>\n<li><strong>Prizepool:<\/strong> Rs.20k<\/li>\n<li><strong>For more enquiries visit<\/strong> : https:\/\/allinput-gamma.vercel.app\/<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Top 3 teams get to keep what they build!!!<\/strong><\/p>","overall_prizes":"Prizepool: \u20b920k","regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":"","registration_clicks":0,"user_id":22299973,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-09-30T09:51:01+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-06T16:26:52+05:30","communication_sent":null,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"dis